      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1902-03-07_WidnesExaminer_art0082" n="art0082">
        <head>SOUTH .EAST LANCASHIRE COMPETITION.</head>
        <p>SOUTH .EAST LANCASHIRE COMPETITION.</p>
        <p>ROCHDaLM HeRNETSI v. BROITGEITON RANGERS. This match was played on the Rochdale Athletic Ground In capital weather, before about 4,000 spectators. The opening stages of the game were rather aurprhing, as the Hornets rushed the ball to the Rangers' line, where Cooper charged down Wilson's kick an 4 scored a try in a very few minutes. After this, however, the game was of a very uninteresting character. The Rangers completely outplayed the Hornets at all positions, and they could haVe simply scored whenever they liked. In the first 11,If they scorea three goals and seven tries, to which they added in the second half one goal and one try, and won a very one-sided game by 32 points to three. Result :—Broughton Rangers, four goals and eight tries (32 points) ; Rochdale Hornets, one try (three points).</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1902-03-07_WidnesExaminer_art0083" n="art0083">
        <p>SOUTH WEST LANCASHIRE LEAGUE.</p>
        <p>LEIGH Y. WIDNES.</p>
        <p>At Leigh. before 3,500 spectators. The game WSB interest- ing and marked by numeroug exciting incidents, but on the whole Widnes had the best of matters and the ssore fairly represents the difference betweee the teams, Leigh playing below their form Widnes ev,ntually won a bard game by a gosl and a try (five points) te a goal (two points.)</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1902-03-07_WidnesExaminer_art0084" n="art0084">
        <head>LANCASHIRE COMBINATION.</head>
        <p>LANCASHIRE COMBINATION.</p>
        <p>WARAING•Tos " A", V SALFORD "A.'</p>
        <p>Played at Warrington on Saturday before a capital gate. Salford kicked off. and the first scrummage was formed inside the home half. Both sides put in sorne tall kicking until the ball was sent into touch. The visitors forced matters and gradually worked their way up the field. The Salford wing man got possession and after tricking several Opponents grounded at the corner. The goal kick failed. Some pretty passing was indulged in by the home forwards in the Salford half, but they could not manage to get through. The pro- ceedings at this stage of the game were favourable to War- rington, and Clare gathering the oval, glided round a cluster of players and dropped a splendid goal just before the inter- val. Half-time arrived with Salford leading by three points to twos The second half was resumed by Warrington in vigorous style. but Salford maintained splendid form,fielding the ball very neatly and repelling many attacks. The visitors did some smart things in kicking and quick following no. Eventually Warrington took up a perm ment position and Salford were hard pressed. Both Bate and Clare made futile efforts to get through, and eventually Lawless had a clear course, but injudiciously kicked dead: Vigorous play was witnessed. Foster (Warrington).suet Dayies(Salford).were ordered off for fighting. Warrington still attacked, without result, and were unluckily beaten by three points to two. ST. HELYS3 CABLE CO. LTD. V WOOLSTON. This match was played on the ground of the latter last Saturday. Nevins. Sixmlth tad Hannion each scored tries for the visitors. Final result ; Cable Company 9 points. Woolstou nil.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1902-03-07_WidnesExaminer_art0085" n="art0085">
        <head>ASSOCIATION FOOTBALL.</head>
        <p>ASSOCIATION FOOTBALL.</p>
        <p>WATRD7GTOS ST. PAVER'S V. LA.TCHFoRD BRITTANIA..</p>
        <p>I Played at Latchford. The home team turned out in fall streigth and scored Ave minutes after the start. St Peter,s thew got possession and rased away with the ball, and from a good centre by Phoenix Craddock put it nicely through. • bit of good play followed, which resulted in Roans scoring a second goal for St Peter's Half-time :St Peter's 2 goals. Brittania 1. The hoc:testers then pre,sed, but the visitors' defenders iccot them well out, and after a hard struggle they scored. St Peter's then had a spell of attacking which ended In Worrall and Craddock scoring third and fou-th goals for St Peter's. Bud-to-end play ensued in which the home team scored. To the surprise of the hemestere St Peter's returned victors by 4 goals to 3.</p>
        <p>WINNINSTG'N ARK V. RA.RLESToWN ROVERS. WARRINGTON CUP—SEMI-FINAL. _ . .</p>
        <p>This inatck was played at Warrington on Saturday, before a poor attendance. Haidestown started, and early on pressed but the Park backs kicked stongly. Half-tirne—Winnington Park 2 goals. Hartestown !Lovers 1. Final : Wilmington, 5 , Barlestown Rovers, I.</p>
        <p>MARLESTOWN V SOLITIIPaRT OPINTRAL.</p>
        <p>This friendly fixture was played at Idarlestown on Saturday In lovely weather. The GentrAl played what was practically he reserve eleven. Half time—No score. Final : EACIOS - own four; SouthportiCentral, nil.</p>
