        <p>efforts, because the doctors in a report which they pre sented the previous day gave the committee a sounding note that the institution would very soon require enlarg- ing. This, of course would entail considerable expense. Councillor BURTON seconded, and the vote was carried. ELECTION OF OFFICERS. The following officers were re-elected :—Councillor John Roberts, chairman ; Mr D Farashaw, deputy- chairman ; Mr J L Tunstall,treasurer; and Mr J Taylor, secretary. foe services rendered by these gentlemen were referred to in warm tenni of praise. Mr Tunstall was unable through illness to be present, and the secre- tary was instructed to convey to bim a message of sympathy and to express a hope that he would bs speedily restored to health. THE STAFF THANKED. The RECTOR proposed a vote of thanks to the honorary medical officers,senior and junior house surgeons,matron and nurses. He said he was quite sure they could never repay the officers of the institution for the unvarying kindness they bestowed upon the patients. (Applause). Mr Fassnaw seconded, and it was carried. Mr ii Wnirs responded and in the course of his re- marks expressed the hope that the members of the uom- mitten would take it upon themselves to make inquiries from time to time as to whether any improvement&amp; could be made in the treatment of the patients. OTHER VOTES OF THANKS. Votes of thanks were passed to the Warrington Rugby Football Club; to Mr T J Dawn and the members of his orchestra (Mr Down's services were very cordially acknowledged); to the Chief Constable and the Police ; to the committee of the May Day procession of horses ; I and to the Press. Alderman MONKS proposed a vote of thanks to the Mayor in his official capicity for his kindness in allow- ing them the use of the Council Chamber,and to him ae I Mr Parr for the kindly interest he always took in what- 'ever was for the welfare of the workingmen of War- rington. (Applause.) I Councillor Jona ROBERTS seconded, and the vote was I heartily carried. The MAYOR having responded the meeting terminated.</p>
